{"author":"Joe Oakhart","author_email":"joeoakhart@navapbc.com","data":{"body":"Regression introduced by this ticket's own AC5 change, now blocking the merge pipeline.\n\n`tests/test_sandbox_capabilities_985f.py::test_sandbox_skip_summary_aggregates_across_xdist_workers` fails on GitHub Actions (`ubuntu-latest, py3.11`):\n\n```\n>       result.assert_outcomes(skipped=2)\nE       AssertionError: assert {'passed': 2,...} == {'passed': 0,...}\ntests/test_sandbox_capabilities_985f.py:241: AssertionError\n```\n\nProvenance, measured: `git log origin/main -S'test_sandbox_skip_summary_aggregates_across_xdist_workers'` returns exactly one commit, `ddb1d953812` \"tests: handle sandbox capability denials\" (2026-09-18 04:41 UTC). That is Gerrit change 2980 as rewritten by rebase-on-submit. The test did not exist on `main` before that merge.\n\nRoot cause: the assertions encode an ambient-host property rather than the behaviour the test is named for. It asserts `skipped=2` plus stdout `\"sandbox ps unavailable: 2\"`, which only holds where `ps` is absent - true inside the sandboxed dev environment, false on a CI runner. Where `ps` is present the two inner tests are not skipped, they pass, and the assertion fails. So the test currently discriminates on the host, not on whether cross-worker skip-summary aggregation works.\n\nBlast radius: this is not confined to its own change. It fails for any patchset, so it has already put `Verified -1` on change 2982 (an unrelated autodeploy fix) and change 2983's run is in flight against the same wall. Every change is blocked until it is fixed.\n\nThis is not a candidate for `recheck`. The failure is deterministic on a runner with `ps` and deterministic in the other direction here; it is a test defect, not an environmental fault.\n\nRemediation in flight. The bar is a test that passes in both environments and still fails if the aggregation logic it guards is broken - not a `skipif` and not a widened assertion."},"env_id":"492a5c71-6cda-48a6-8134-02ff6a672739","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1789721961150693001,"uuid":"4f5ba24f-b3d2-4a8e-8611-98749c5d9a7c"}